  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MHPSS Technical Group Co-coordinator - World Health Organization Hungary</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Assignment at the request of WHO for a MHPSS Technical Group Co-coordinator of an MHPSS coordination focal point in Budapest, Hungary. The task includes coordination MHPSS response with partners in Hungary and neighbouring countries Slovakia and Romania. All those three countries are establishing multi-sectoral response mechanisms and are asking to be provided with guidelines on policies, plans and evidence based interventions. Those countries would need good coordination capacity so that the many partners that are being mobilized at global, regional and local level to assist the displaced, migrants and refugees, would be coordinated amongst, aligned with the IASC MHPSS guidelines and coherent in using the MHPSS resources.Both aims of MHPSS22001 (Hungary) and MHPSS22003 (Poland) were to promote that Mental Health and Psychosocial Support (MHPSS) was well integrated within the Ukraine refugee response in Hungary and Poland. At the beginning of 2022, several thousand Ukrainian families have fled their residence towards the western border of the country that neighbors with Moldova, Romania, Hungary, Slovakia, Poland, and Belarus. Worth noting that most of the neighboring countries to Ukraine were not coping with an emergency in decades and hence felt ill-equipped to face the demands of a humanitarian situation, including their capacities to respond to psycho-social needs of migrants and refugees. For this this reason, the MHPSS Surge Mechanism from The Netherlands Enterprise Agency (RVO) has provided support by deploying two experts to Hungary and Poland. This is why it is good to report these projects to IATI.</narrative>
  </description>
